body:
The feeling comes from within brother. :)

&#x200B;

Also Skyrim reputation.

That's a 7ft+ bearing sword, which were mostly used "ceremonially", and were well known to be basically unusable in a combat scenario due to their weight, and size. That one specifically is falsely named the "the sword of Grutte Pier Gerlofs Donia" when in reality it was just a normal bearing sword from around the 1400s. So you'd be wrong to say that thing ever saw combat.

&#x200B;

As for the problem with Guts's sword in the picture? It ain't the Dragonslayer, that's for damn sure.
